WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.009
Rosa paid Social Security taxes for twenty years, which earned her work credits.

00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:12.479
To qualify for Social Security disability insurance she must be insured: generally 40 credits,

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:18.950
with 20 earned in the ten years before disability, and fewer for younger workers.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:22.185
She must also meet the program’s definition.

00:00:22.185 --> 00:00:26.807
Social Security is funded by payroll taxes and administered federally,

00:00:26.807 --> 00:00:31.429
and its disability benefit is an earned benefit, not welfare.

00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:35.127
A separate program, Supplemental Security Income, serves disabled

00:00:35.127 --> 00:00:38.825
people with little work history and limited means.

00:00:38.825 --> 00:00:42.060
Most exam questions concern the insurance program.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.158
Social Security pays only for total disability.

00:00:45.158 --> 00:00:50.910
The claimant must be unable to engage in any substantial gainful activity because

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:56.662
of a medically determinable physical or mental impairment that has lasted or is

00:00:56.662 --> 00:01:01.972
expected to last at least twelve months or to result in death.

00:01:01.972 --> 00:01:05.512
Substantial gainful activity is measured by a monthly

00:01:05.512 --> 00:01:08.610
earnings threshold that is indexed each year.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:11.708
There are no partial or short-term benefits.

00:01:11.708 --> 00:01:15.248
Rosa, who could manage a store, would be

00:01:15.248 --> 00:01:18.345
denied even though her own-occupation policy pays.

00:01:18.345 --> 00:01:24.540
That gap is exactly what the social insurance supplement rider in Lesson 30 addresses.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.923
Benefits begin after a five-month waiting period, so the

00:01:27.923 --> 00:01:31.307
first payment covers the sixth full month of disability.

00:01:31.307 --> 00:01:35.818
The monthly amount is the worker’s primary insurance amount, the same figure

00:01:35.818 --> 00:01:39.953
used for retirement at full retirement age, based on lifetime earnings.

00:01:39.953 --> 00:01:44.089
Eligible family members, a spouse caring for young children and dependent

00:01:44.089 --> 00:01:47.848
children, may receive additional benefits subject to a family maximum.

00:01:47.848 --> 00:01:53.111
After 24 months of disability benefits the worker qualifies for Medicare regardless of age.

00:01:53.111 --> 00:01:56.871
Benefits continue while the disability lasts, with periodic reviews and

00:01:56.871 --> 00:02:00.630
work incentives that let a recipient test returning to work.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:03.026
Workers compensation is a state system.

00:02:03.026 --> 00:02:07.020
In Maryland nearly every employer must carry it, through a

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:11.014
private insurer, the Chesapeake Employers’ Insurance Company or approved self-insurance.

00:02:11.014 --> 00:02:14.608
It covers employees for accidental injuries and occupational diseases

00:02:14.608 --> 00:02:18.203
arising out of and in the course of employment.

00:02:18.203 --> 00:02:23.394
It is no-fault: the worker need not prove the employer was negligent, and

00:02:23.394 --> 00:02:28.187
the employer is protected from most lawsuits by the exclusive remedy rule.

00:02:28.187 --> 00:02:31.382
Rosa, self-employed with no employees, is not covered

00:02:31.382 --> 00:02:34.577
unless she elects coverage; Priya’s twenty employees are.

00:02:34.577 --> 00:02:38.970
Independent contractors are generally excluded, which is why the classification matters.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:44.444
Maryland workers compensation pays medical expenses for the work injury without dollar limits.

00:02:44.444 --> 00:02:49.497
It pays wage replacement: temporary total disability at two-thirds of the average

00:02:49.497 --> 00:02:54.551
weekly wage, up to a state maximum, while the worker recovers; temporary

00:02:54.551 --> 00:02:59.604
partial while working at reduced pay; permanent partial disability on a schedule

00:02:59.604 --> 00:03:04.657
for lasting impairments; and permanent total disability for the most serious injuries.

00:03:04.657 --> 00:03:10.131
It funds vocational rehabilitation and pays death benefits to dependents plus funeral expenses.

00:03:10.131 --> 00:03:13.500
Disputes go to the Maryland Workers’ Compensation Commission.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.290
Benefits are tax-free, and private disability policies offset them.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.302
Think of the three systems as layers.

00:03:20.302 --> 00:03:25.036
Workers compensation pays first for job injuries, quickly and without fault.

00:03:25.036 --> 00:03:28.909
Social Security pays for total, long-lasting disability from any

00:03:28.909 --> 00:03:32.351
cause, after five months and a strict test.

00:03:32.351 --> 00:03:37.945
Private disability income fills the gaps: injuries off the job, disabilities that are

00:03:37.945 --> 00:03:43.540
partial or occupation-specific, the five-month wait and the years before Social Security decides.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:46.982
Group plans offset the government benefits; individual policies

00:03:46.982 --> 00:03:50.425
generally pay in full, with riders that coordinate.

00:03:50.425 --> 00:03:53.867
A producer who knows the public programs can

00:03:53.867 --> 00:03:57.310
show exactly which gap each private dollar covers.
